import{_ as i,o as t,c as a,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Housing Security Law","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/45-住房保障法.md","filePath":"en/45-住房保障法.md"}'),o={name:"en/45-住房保障法.md"};function s(r,e,l,d,h,c){return t(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="housing-security-law" tabindex="-1">Housing Security Law <a class="header-anchor" href="#housing-security-law" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Housing Security Law&quot;">​</a></h1><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Content</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Document No.</td><td>45</td></tr><tr><td>Module</td><td>Legal System and Governance Framework</td></tr><tr><td>Core Keywords</td><td>Right of residence, Guaranteed housing, Spatial legal principles, Livable environment, Anti-speculation</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="i-legislative-purpose-and-basic-principles" tabindex="-1">I. Legislative Purpose and Basic Principles <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-legislative-purpose-and-basic-principles" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Legislative Purpose and Basic Principles&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The <em>Housing Security Law</em> is one of the five supporting laws of the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization. It aims to guarantee the right of residence of all lives within the Hengyuan Universe, establish a fair and sustainable housing security system, use spatial legal principle dispatch technology to provide suitable living spaces for all races, and prevent speculation and predation in the housing sector.</p><p>This Law establishes the following basic principles:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Principle</th><th>Connotation</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Residence Guarantee</td><td>Every life has the right to obtain suitable living space; the state and civilization have the obligation to guarantee basic residence needs</td></tr><tr><td>Public Welfare Priority</td><td>Housing is first a necessity of life rather than a speculative commodity; guaranteed housing has a public welfare attribute</td></tr><tr><td>Spatial Efficiency</td><td>Use spatial legal principle dispatch technology to improve spatial utilization efficiency and expand livable space</td></tr><tr><td>Non-Human Adaptation</td><td>Provide adapted living spaces for the physiological characteristics and living habits of different races</td></tr><tr><td>Livable Environment</td><td>Living spaces should possess a good ecological environment, infrastructure, and public services</td></tr><tr><td>Anti-Speculation</td><td>Prohibit speculative profiteering with housing as the target, preventing housing from becoming a tool for plundering wealth</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="ii-legal-guarantees-of-the-right-of-residence" tabindex="-1">II. Legal Guarantees of the Right of Residence <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-legal-guarantees-of-the-right-of-residence" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Legal Guarantees of the Right of Residence&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This Law explicitly stipulates that the right of residence is a basic right conferred upon every life by the Symbiotic Constitution, specifically including:</p><ol><li><strong>Basic Right of Residence</strong>: Every life has the right to obtain living space not lower than the minimum standard, with the minimum standard determined according to racial body size and living needs.</li><li><strong>Right to Apply for Guaranteed Housing</strong>: Eligible lives have the right to apply for guaranteed housing, with application conditions and allocation standards open and transparent.</li><li><strong>Right to Residence Safety</strong>: Living spaces should meet safety standards; dangerous buildings and unsuitable living spaces shall not be rented or allocated.</li><li><strong>Right to Residence Stability</strong>: Residents of guaranteed housing enjoy stable residence rights when meeting conditions and shall not be arbitrarily evicted.</li><li><strong>Right to Living Environment</strong>: Residents have the right to obtain clean air, water sources, and a good surrounding environment, and have the right to file complaints about environmental pollution.</li><li><strong>Right to Housing Renovation</strong>: Residents have the right to reasonably renovate their living spaces on the premise of not affecting building safety and the rights of others.</li></ol><h2 id="iii-housing-security-system" tabindex="-1">III. Housing Security System <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-housing-security-system" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Housing Security System&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The housing security system of the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization is divided into three types of housing, covering different levels of demand:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Name</th><th>Guaranteed Group</th><th>Allocation Method</th><th>Rent/Price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>First type</td><td>Public Rental Housing</td><td>Low-income groups, junior cultivators, new immigrants</td><td>Application and review system, queued allocation</td><td>Symbolic low rent</td></tr><tr><td>Second type</td><td>Shared Ownership Housing</td><td>Middle-income groups, intermediate cultivators</td><td>Application and review system, lottery allocation</td><td>Below market price, shared ownership between individual and state</td></tr><tr><td>Third type</td><td>Commercial Housing</td><td>High-income groups, advanced cultivators</td><td>Market transaction</td><td>Market price, subject to regulation</td></tr></tbody></table><p>In addition, spatial legal principle dispatch technology is used to build &quot;folded space residential zones&quot;: expanding the residential area in limited physical space through space-folding technology, providing more living space for high-density areas. Folded space residential zones must undergo safety assessment to ensure spatial stability.</p><h2 id="iv-housing-adaptation-for-non-human-races" tabindex="-1">IV. Housing Adaptation for Non-Human Races <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-housing-adaptation-for-non-human-races" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Housing Adaptation for Non-Human Races&quot;">​</a></h2><p>In response to the special residence needs of different races within the Hengyuan Universe, this Law establishes a housing adaptation institution for non-human races:</p><ul><li><strong>Aquatic races</strong>: Provided with underwater living spaces or amphibious residences, equipped with water circulation and water quality maintenance systems.</li><li><strong>Flying races</strong>: Provided with high-altitude living spaces or residences with takeoff and landing platforms, equipped with air traffic management.</li><li><strong>Energy lives</strong>: Provided with living spaces of suitable energy concentration, equipped with energy stabilization devices.</li><li><strong>Giant races</strong>: Provided with large-scale living spaces, with building structures specially reinforced.</li><li><strong>Microscopic races</strong>: Provided with microscopic residential zones, equipped with scaling passages and dedicated facilities.</li></ul><p>Non-human housing adaptation standards are jointly formulated by the housing competent authority together with representatives of all races and updated regularly.</p><h2 id="v-housing-construction-and-management" tabindex="-1">V. Housing Construction and Management <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-housing-construction-and-management" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Housing Construction and Management&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Housing Construction Planning</strong>: The state formulates housing construction plans based on population growth and immigration, ensuring a balance between housing supply and demand.</li><li><strong>Construction Standards</strong>: The construction of guaranteed housing must meet safety, environmental protection, and livability standards; lowering construction quality is prohibited.</li><li><strong>Property Management</strong>: Residential areas implement a model combining autonomous management and professional property services; residents have the right to participate in property management decisions.</li><li><strong>Housing Maintenance</strong>: The maintenance of guaranteed housing is the responsibility of the housing management institution, with maintenance funds drawn from public accumulation.</li><li><strong>Exit Mechanism</strong>: Residents of guaranteed housing whose income or cultivation exceeds the guarantee standard should exit the guaranteed housing or convert to commercial housing, with a reasonable transition period granted for exit.</li></ul><h2 id="vi-anti-speculation-and-supervision" tabindex="-1">VI. Anti-Speculation and Supervision <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-anti-speculation-and-supervision" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Anti-Speculation and Supervision&quot;">​</a></h2><p>To prevent speculation and predation in the housing sector, this Law establishes the following supervision measures:</p><ol><li>Limit the number of commercial housing units held by individuals; progressive property taxes are levied on amounts exceeding the limit.</li><li>Prohibit the subletting and resale of guaranteed housing; violators have their guarantee eligibility revoked and housing recovered.</li><li>Establish a public information system for housing transactions, preventing behind-the-scenes operations and price manipulation.</li><li>Implement qualification management and fund supervision for real estate developers, preventing unfinished projects and fraud.</li><li>Establish housing complaint and dispute resolution mechanisms, protecting the lawful rights and interests of residents.</li></ol><h2 id="vii-legal-liability" tabindex="-1">VII. Legal Liability <a class="header-anchor" href="#vii-legal-liability" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VII. Legal Liability&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Acts violating the provisions of this Law shall bear the following liabilities depending on the severity of the circumstances:</p><ul><li>Those who allocate guaranteed housing in violation of regulations shall be ordered to correct and the responsible persons disciplined.</li><li>Those who sublet or resell guaranteed housing shall have their guarantee eligibility revoked, housing recovered, and be fined.</li><li>Developers who lower construction quality shall be ordered to rework and fined; in serious circumstances, their qualifications shall be revoked.</li><li>Those engaged in housing speculation shall be subject to high speculation taxes and fines.</li><li>Those who rent dangerous buildings causing harm to residents shall bear compensation liability; in serious circumstances, criminal liability shall be pursued.</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The <em>Housing Security Law</em> is the implementation of the &quot;a path for everyone&quot; philosophy of the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization in the residence domain. By establishing a classified housing security system, using spatial legal principle technology to expand living space, adapting to the residence needs of non-human races, and combating housing speculation, it ensures that every life can have a safe, suitable, and stable home, providing secure residence guarantees for the joint advancement of all races.</p><h2 id="related-documents" tabindex="-1">Related Documents <a class="header-anchor" href="#related-documents" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related Documents&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>40-共生宪法总纲 (Symbiotic Constitution: General Principles)</li><li>39-住房与环境保障 (Housing and Environmental Protection)</li><li>13-空间法理调度体系详解 (Detailed Explanation of the Spatial Legal Principle Dispatch System)</li><li>46-环境保护法 (Environmental Protection Law)</li></ul>',29)])])}const p=i(o,[["render",s]]);export{g as __pageData,p as default};
